      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_tab_tBJXhQ": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "IRREGULAR PERIODS OR PCOS?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p><strong>PCOS symptoms aren’t just hormonal. They’re metabolic.</strong> In two 12-week studies of women with PCOS, myo-inositol significantly lowered insulin and testosterone.*</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_zJaULT": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "CRAVINGS AND BLOOD SUGAR DIPS?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>The 3pm crash isn’t about willpower. <strong>It’s how your body is handling insulin.</strong> Inositol is a compound your body already makes and uses to pass on the insulin signal. Cravings and food noise are the first thing our customers mention.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_EHUzbD": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "MOOD DIPS BEFORE YOUR PERIOD?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p><strong>Mood dips before your period aren’t a character flaw.</strong> Blood sugar and hormones are connected, and both respond to how your body handles insulin. That’s the signal inositol supports.*</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_AmTzjg": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "CAME OFF THE PILL AND STILL WAITING?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Stopped the pill and still waiting for your cycle? <strong>Inositol is a compound your body already makes.</strong> You’re not adding something foreign. You’re topping up something that’s meant to be there.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_9mhfxD": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "TRYING TO CONCEIVE?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>It’s not only hormones. <strong>How your body handles insulin affects ovulation too.</strong> Inositol supports healthy ovulation.*</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_xVREzb": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "LOW ENERGY AND CRASHES?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Exhausted after eight hours of sleep? It may be blood sugar, not laziness. In a 6-month trial, HOMA-IR, a measure of how the body responds to insulin, <strong>fell 75%</strong> with 4g of myo-inositol a day plus diet.*</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
