            "bf_studies_in_note": true,
            "bf_studies_label": "*See the studies",
            "bf_footnote": "<p>*Studies of myo-inositol, not of Bodology. Genazzani et al. 2008 and Artini et al. 2013 (Gynecological Endocrinology): overweight women with PCOS (20 and 50 enrolled) took 2g of myo-inositol with folic acid daily for 12 weeks, half the amount in a daily serving of Bodology. The researchers reported significantly lower insulin and testosterone.</p><p>Giordano et al. 2011 (Menopause): 80 postmenopausal women with metabolic syndrome followed a diet with either 4g of myo-inositol a day or placebo for 6 months. The researchers reported that HOMA-IR, a measure of how the body responds to insulin, fell 75% in the myo-inositol group, significantly more than with diet and placebo.</p><p>Results in studies may not reflect individual outcomes. These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.</p>",
            "bf_servings_per_tub": 45,
