            "bf_tier_1_link_text": "",
            "bf_tier_1_link_tier": "2",
            "bf_tier_1_study_title": "What 3 months looked like in the research",
            "bf_tier_1_study_text": "<p>Women with PCOS took myo-inositol daily for 12 weeks. Insulin and testosterone both fell significantly. The control group saw no change.<br/><br/>Genazzani et al., 2008 · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080/09513590801893232\">Read the study</a><br/>Artini et al., 2013 · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3109/09513590.2012.743020\">Read the study</a></p>",
            "bf_tier_1_footnote": "*Studies of myo-inositol, not of Bodology. Genazzani et al. 2008 and Artini et al. 2013 (Gynecological Endocrinology): overweight women with PCOS (20 and 50 enrolled) took 2g of myo-inositol with folic acid daily for 12 weeks, half the amount in a daily serving of Bodology. The researchers reported significantly lower insulin and testosterone. Results in studies may not reflect individual outcomes. These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.",
            "bf_tier_2_label": "6 month bundle",
