            "bf_tier_2_title": "6-Month Bundle",
            "bf_tier_2_badge": "6-month trial",
            "bf_tier_2_badge_style": "navy",
            "bf_tier_2_note": "Give it the full 6 months the clinical research used*",
            "bf_tier_2_link_text": "",
            "bf_tier_2_link_tier": "3",
            "bf_tier_2_study_title": "What 6 months looked like in the research",
            "bf_tier_2_study_text": "<p>In a 6-month study, 80 postmenopausal women with metabolic syndrome followed a diet with 4g of myo-inositol a day or placebo. That is the same daily myo-inositol as two scoops of Bodology®, though the study did not use Bodology. HOMA-IR, a standard marker of insulin resistance, fell 75% in the myo-inositol group, significantly more than with placebo. The researchers also reported changes in blood pressure, triglycerides and HDL cholesterol.<br/><br/>Giordano et al., 2011 · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1097/gme.0b013e3181e8e1b1\">Read the study</a></p>",
            "bf_tier_2_footnote": "*Study of myo-inositol, not of Bodology. Giordano et al. 2011 (Menopause): 80 postmenopausal women with metabolic syndrome followed a diet with either 4g of myo-inositol a day or placebo for 6 months. The researchers reported that HOMA-IR, a measure of how the body responds to insulin, fell 75% in the myo-inositol group, significantly more than with diet and placebo. Results in studies may not reflect individual outcomes. These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.",
