            "bf_tier_3_tubs": 8,
            "bf_tier_3_months": 12,
            "bf_tier_3_pct": 55,
            "bf_tier_3_free_text": "~7 months free",
            "bf_tier_3_tubs_free_text": "",
            "bf_tier_3_title": "12-month supply",
            "bf_tier_3_badge": "Best value",
            "bf_tier_3_badge_style": "lavender",
            "bf_tier_3_note": "In the 12-month trial, 1 in 5 women no longer had metabolic syndrome*",
            "bf_tier_3_link_text": "",
            "bf_tier_3_link_tier": "0",
            "bf_tier_3_study_title": "What a year looked like in the research",
            "bf_tier_3_study_text": "<p>80 women with metabolic syndrome, all showing insulin resistance, took 4g of inositol a day alongside diet. The same daily amount as two scoops of Bodology®.</p><p>After 12 months, 8 of the 40 women taking inositol no longer met the criteria for metabolic syndrome. In the diet-only group it was only 1 of 40.<br/><br/>Santamaria et al., 2012 · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3109/13697137.2011.631063\">Read the study</a></p>",
