    "why_inositol_home": {
      "type": "why-inositol",
      "blocks": {
        "text_JCbbfq": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Why Bodology® inositol?</p><p>The full 4g dose the studies used.*</p>",
            "size": 30
          }
        },
        "text_cHr3qn": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Bodology® delivers the full clinically studied daily dose — 4,000mg myo-inositol and 100mg D-chiro-inositol at the 40:1 ratio used in research — in one unflavored serving.*</p>",
            "size": 0
          }
        },
        "accordion_Yfz7fg": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "WHAT'S INSIDE",
            "open": false,
            "chips": "4,000mg myo-inositol\n100mg D-chiro-inositol\n40:1 ratio\nNo fillers\nVegan\nGluten-free",
            "text": ""
          }
        },
        "stat_b6qWpy": {
          "type": "stat",
          "settings": {
            "value": "-75%",
            "text": "<p>insulin resistance (HOMA index) after 6 months on 4g a day, postmenopausal women*</p>"
          }
        },
        "stat_t4fBEx": {
          "type": "stat",
          "settings": {
            "value": "1 in 5",
            "text": "<p>women no longer had metabolic syndrome after 12 months on inositol. On diet alone, 1 in 40*</p>"
          }
        },
        "stat_8HwQip": {
          "type": "stat",
          "settings": {
            "value": "+22%",
            "text": "<p>HDL ('good') cholesterol after 6 months*</p>"
          }
        },
        "stat_Aqd3H4": {
          "type": "stat",
          "settings": {
            "value": "−20%",
            "text": "<p>triglycerides after 6 months*</p>"
          }
        },
        "footer_Dk8jFD": {
          "type": "footer",
          "settings": {
            "position": "right",
            "studies_link_text": "See the studies",
            "popup_title": "The studies behind these numbers",
            "popup_text": "<h4>What 6 months looked like in the research</h4><p>In a 6-month study, 80 postmenopausal women with metabolic syndrome followed a diet with 4g of myo-inositol a day or placebo. That is the same daily myo-inositol as two scoops of Bodology®, though the study did not use Bodology. HOMA-IR, a standard marker of insulin resistance, fell 75% in the myo-inositol group, significantly more than with placebo. The researchers also reported changes in blood pressure, triglycerides and HDL cholesterol.<br/><br/>Giordano et al., 2011 · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1097/gme.0b013e3181e8e1b1\">Read the study</a></p><h4>What a year looked like in the research</h4><p>80 women with metabolic syndrome, all showing insulin resistance, took 4g of inositol a day alongside diet. The same daily amount as two scoops of Bodology®.</p><p>After 12 months, 8 of the 40 women taking inositol no longer met the criteria for metabolic syndrome. In the diet-only group it was only 1 of 40.<br/><br/>Santamaria et al., 2012 · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3109/13697137.2011.631063\">Read the study</a></p><h4>What 3 months looked like in the research</h4><p>Women with PCOS took myo-inositol daily for 12 weeks. Insulin and testosterone both fell significantly. The control group saw no change.<br/><br/>Genazzani et al., 2008 · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080/09513590801893232\">Read the study</a><br/>Artini et al., 2013 · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3109/09513590.2012.743020\">Read the study</a></p>",
            "popup_small": "*Giordano et al., 2011 (Menopause): 80 postmenopausal women with metabolic syndrome. Results in studies may not reflect individual outcomes. Trial did not involve Bodology® products. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.\n*Santamaria et al. 2012 (Climacteric): 80 postmenopausal women with metabolic syndrome. Results in studies may not reflect individual outcomes. Trial did not involve Bodology® products. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.\n*Genazzani et al. 2008 and Artini et al. 2013 (Gynecol Endocrinol). Results in studies may not reflect individual outcomes. Trial did not involve Bodology® products. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.",
            "text": "<p>*These statements have not been evaluated by the FDA. These studies did not use Bodology® Inositol specifically. [studies]</p>"
          }
        }
      },
